			"notes": "## Added\n- **NeoForge support.** The mod is now available for both **Fabric** and **NeoForge**.\n- **Multi-version support:** Minecraft **26.1.2**, **26.2**, and **26.3**.\n\n## Changed\n- The Continue button now uses Minecraft's built-in `gui.continue` label, so it is localized in **every** language the game supports. The mod's own bundled translations were removed.\n- Build system migrated to **Stonecutter** with **Architectury Loom**; each loader/version now builds a separate jar named `continue-button-continued-<loader>-<version>.jar` (e.g. `continue-button-continued-fabric-1.1.0+26.3.jar`).\n- Internal rewrite: the title-screen mixin was removed in favor of Architectury's cross-loader events (`ClientGuiEvent`, `ClientTickEvent`, `ClientPlayerEvent`).\n\n## Fixed\n- **No more freezing/lagging on the main menu when the saved server is down** ([#1](https://github.com/Likos-Lupus/continue-button-continued/issues/1)). The status ping now runs off the render thread and only once per title screen.\n- The Continue button's tooltip now shows *\"Can't connect to server\"* when the saved server is unreachable, instead of being stuck on *\"pinging\"*.\n- Clicking Continue on a known-down server now shows a clean *\"Failed to connect to the server\"* screen instead of leaking the raw connection exception (`finishConnect(..) failed with error(-111): Connection refused`).\n- Fixed a race where a ping started for a previous title screen could overwrite the current screen's status.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Requires **Architectury API** (Fabric or NeoForge build) at runtime. On Fabric, **Fabric API** is also required (pulled in by Architectury API).\n- NeoForge 26.3 currently tracks NeoForge `26.3.0.46-beta`.\n\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/Likos-Lupus/continue-button-continued/compare/1.0.0+26.3...1.1.0"
		},
